<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>DiscoveryOS | Dana Kreisberg</title><meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin><link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter+Tight:ital,wght@0,300;0,400;0,500;1,100;1,300;1,400&family=Inter:wght@300;400;500&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400&display=swap" rel="stylesheet"><style is:global>
:root{--paper:#fff;--paper-2:#f2f2f2;--ink:oklch(14% .01 240);--ink-60:oklch(14% .01 240/.62);--ink-40:oklch(14% .01 240/.42);--rule:oklch(14% .01 240/.14);--display:"Inter Tight",sans-serif;--body:"Inter",sans-serif;--mono:"JetBrains Mono",monospace;--gutter:8%;--bagel-purple:#5C5CEB}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font-family:var(--body);-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased}img{display:block;max-width:100%}p,h1,h2,h3{margin:0}.meta,.step-num,.decision-mono,.exploration-kicker{font:11px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-40)}.title-section{padding:64px var(--gutter) 56px}.title-meta{margin-bottom:40px}.cs-h1{font:400 clamp(48px,7vw,96px)/.95 var(--display);letter-spacing:-.04em}.cs-h1 em{font-weight:100;font-style:italic;color:var(--bagel-purple)}.lede{max-width:62ch;margin-top:40px;color:var(--ink-60);font-size:19px;line-height:1.5}.see-in-action-link{display:inline-block;margin-top:16px;color:var(--ink);font-size:15px;font-weight:500}.meta-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:32px;margin-top:64px;padding-top:24px;border-top:1px solid var(--rule)}.meta-val{margin-top:8px;font-size:15px}.section{padding:96px var(--gutter)}.section-alt{padding:100px var(--gutter);background:var(--paper-2);border-block:1px solid var(--rule)}.cs-h2{max-width:16ch;font:400 clamp(36px,3.8vw,60px)/1.02 var(--display);letter-spacing:-.03em}.cs-h2-wide{max-width:23ch;margin-top:16px;font:400 clamp(40px,4.4vw,72px)/1.02 var(--display);letter-spacing:-.032em}.body-text{max-width:58ch;color:var(--ink-60);font-size:16px;line-height:1.65}.body-text+.body-text{margin-top:16px}.two-col,.feat-split{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.1fr;gap:64px;align-items:start}.feat-split{grid-template-columns:1fr 1.4fr;gap:56px}.img-frame{display:flex;flex-direction:column}.img-frame img{width:100%;border:0;border-radius:12px}.fig-cap{padding-top:10px;color:var(--ink-40);font-size:13px;line-height:1.45}.stat-row,.outcomes-bold{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);margin-top:56px;border-top:1px solid var(--rule)}.stat{padding:40px 32px 40px 0}.stat-n{padding-top:24px;font:400 clamp(64px,8vw,128px)/1 var(--display);letter-spacing:-.04em}.stat-d{font-size:.45em;color:var(--ink-40)}.stat-l{max-width:27ch;margin-top:18px;color:var(--ink-60);font-size:15px;line-height:1.5}.reframe-statement{max-width:25ch;margin-top:48px;font:clamp(2rem,4vw,4rem)/1.03 var(--display);letter-spacing:-.035em}.act-divider{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:24px;padding:56px var(--gutter) 48px;border-block:1px solid var(--rule)}.act-num{font:10px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-40)}.act-title{font:300 clamp(2.4rem,6vw,5.2rem)/1.04 var(--display);letter-spacing:-.03em}.workflow-line{margin-top:32px;color:var(--bagel-purple);font:clamp(1.35rem,2.5vw,2.2rem)/1.25 var(--display);letter-spacing:-.025em}.exploration-grid,.walkthrough-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:48px;margin-top:48px}.exploration-card{padding:28px;border:0;border-radius:12px;background:var(--paper)}.exploration-card .img-frame,.walkthrough-step .img-frame{margin-top:24px}.exploration-title,.walkthrough-title{margin-top:12px;font:400 clamp(1.5rem,2.5vw,2.25rem)/1.05 var(--display);letter-spacing:-.025em}.walkthrough-step{padding-top:20px;border-top:1px solid var(--rule)}.outcome-item{padding:32px;border-right:1px solid var(--rule)}.outcome-item:first-child{padding-left:0}.outcome-item:last-child{border:0}.outcome-stat{color:var(--bagel-purple);font:300 clamp(2rem,4vw,3.5rem)/1 var(--display);letter-spacing:-.03em}.outcome-label{max-width:22ch;margin-top:12px;color:var(--ink-60);font-size:14px;line-height:1.5}.outcome-footnote{margin-top:20px;color:var(--ink-40);font-size:12px;font-style:italic}.closing{padding:140px var(--gutter);color:#e6e6e7;background:#0b0b0d}.closing-kicker{font:11px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#ffffff80}.closing-quote{max-width:26ch;margin-top:32px;font:300 clamp(26px,3.5vw,56px)/1.15 var(--display);letter-spacing:-.03em}.closing-quote em{font-style:italic}@media(max-width:900px){:root{--gutter:5%}.two-col,.feat-split,.exploration-grid,.walkthrough-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:40px}.stat-row,.outcomes-bold,.meta-row{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}@media(max-width:600px){:root{--gutter:20px}.section,.section-alt{padding-block:72px}.stat-row,.outcomes-bold,.meta-row{grid-template-columns:1fr}.outcome-item,.outcome-item:first-child{padding:28px 0;border-right:0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}.act-divider{gap:14px;padding-block:40px}}
.img-frame video{width:100%;border:0;border-radius:12px;background:#0e0e14}
.stat-row{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.design-decisions > .cs-h2-wide{margin-bottom:64px}.design-principle{align-items:start}.design-principle + .design-principle{padding-top:56px;border-top:1px solid var(--rule)} .cs-h2-wide + .body-text{margin-top:32px}.stat-row{border-top:0}.gap-callout{max-width:72ch;margin-top:64px;padding:32px;border-radius:20px;background:var(--paper-2)}.gap-callout .reframe-statement{margin-top:0}.gap-callout .body-text{margin-top:24px}.os-accent{color:var(--bagel-purple)}.principle-one .img-frame{width:70%;justify-self:end}.section:nth-of-type(2) .img-frame img{border-top:0!important;outline:0}@media(max-width:900px){.principle-one .img-frame{width:100%;justify-self:stretch}} </style></head><body><Nav />
<section class="title-section"><div class="title-meta"><span class="meta">Case Study · Bagel.AI</span></div><h1 class="cs-h1">Discovery<em>OS</em></h1><p class="lede">Bagel.AI brings customer evidence together for product teams. I redesigned Discovery around a simple question: how can Bagel help PMs figure out what deserves their attention?</p><a href="https://bagel.ai/platform-overview/bagel-discovery-os/#See-it-in-action" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="see-in-action-link">See it in action ↗</a><div class="meta-row"><div><span class="meta">Role</span><div class="meta-val">UX Design &amp; Strategy</div></div><div><span class="meta">Scope</span><div class="meta-val">End-to-end product redesign</div></div><div><span class="meta">Year</span><div class="meta-val">2025 · NDA</div></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><span class="meta">01 · Context</span><div class="two-col" style="margin-top:16px"><div><h2 class="cs-h2">PMs had the signals. They still had to connect the dots.</h2></div><div><p class="body-text">Bagel brings together customer calls, support tickets, CRM data, feature requests, and other customer evidence.</p><p class="body-text">PMs could look at this evidence by customer, trend, or business impact. But they still had to connect those views themselves to answer a basic question: <strong>what should we build next?</strong></p></div></div><div class="img-frame" style="margin-top:48px"><img src="/images/bagelOS-01-four-spaces.png" alt="Four Bagel product spaces and the question of what to build next"><div class="fig-cap">Evidence was organized by KPI, customer, and trends, but not around the PM's next decision.</div></div></section>
<section class="section-alt"><span class="meta">02 · Evidence</span><h2 class="cs-h2-wide">Discovery wasn't leading anywhere.</h2><p class="body-text">Discovery queries were often broad and exploratory rather than precise searches. PMs were looking for patterns and opportunities, but very few of those searches turned into an Idea.</p><div class="stat-row"><div class="stat"><div class="stat-n">4.4<span class="stat-d">%</span></div><div class="stat-l">of Discovery queries converted to an Idea</div></div><div class="stat"><div class="stat-n">~140</div><div class="stat-l">average weekly Idea page views, while Discovery saw almost no usage</div></div></div><p class="reframe-statement">The problem wasn't a missing feature. It was a missing workflow.</p></section>
<div class="act-divider" style="background:var(--paper-2)"><span class="act-num">Part 01</span><h2 class="act-title">Research</h2></div><section class="section-alt"><span class="meta">03 · Understanding the PM workflow</span><h2 class="cs-h2-wide">How do PMs actually get from signals to a decision?</h2><p class="body-text">Instead of starting with the existing Discovery experience, I mapped how PMs work with customer evidence more broadly.</p><p class="body-text">The process was a loop: gather signals, investigate, make sense of what they found, prioritize, build, and measure the result.</p><p class="body-text">Discovery wasn't one search step. It happened throughout that process.</p><div class="img-frame" style="margin-top:48px"><img src="/images/bagelOS-02-pm-workflow.png" alt="PM prioritization loop and three jobs to be done"><div class="fig-cap">The PM prioritization loop: gather signals, investigate, make sense, prioritize, build a roadmap, and measure.</div></div></section>
<section class="section" style="padding-bottom:48px"><span class="meta">04 · Exploration</span><h2 class="cs-h2-wide">Where should Bagel fit?</h2><p class="body-text">I explored two directions to understand which part of this process Bagel should support.</p><div class="exploration-grid"><article class="exploration-card"><span class="exploration-kicker">Direction 01</span><h3 class="exploration-title">Add structure within an Idea</h3><p class="body-text" style="margin-top:16px">One direction added Top Themes to an existing Idea. The themes grouped verified customer evidence so PMs could understand what was driving the Idea.</p><p class="body-text">It made an existing Idea easier to investigate, but it started too late. The PM already had to know what they wanted to look into.</p><div class="img-frame"><img src="/images/bagelOS-03-exploration-themes.png" alt="Top Themes within an existing Idea"></div></article><article class="exploration-card"><span class="exploration-kicker">Direction 02</span><h3 class="exploration-title">Could Bagel become a planning tool?</h3><p class="body-text" style="margin-top:16px">I also explored taking Bagel further into prioritization and roadmap planning.</p><p class="body-text">This went too far in the other direction. PMs already had tools for planning, and Bagel didn't have all the business context needed to replace them.</p><div class="img-frame"><img src="/images/bagelOS-04-exploration-roadmap.png" alt="Exploration of a roadmap and planning direction"></div></article></div><div class="gap-callout"><p class="reframe-statement">The explorations clarified the product role.</p><p class="body-text">Bagel didn't need to help PMs organize an Idea they already had or replace their planning tool. It needed to help them figure out what <strong>was worth investigating in the first place.</strong></p></div></section>
<section class="section-alt" style="background:#fff;border-top:0;padding-top:56px"><span class="meta">05 · The opportunity</span><h2 class="cs-h2-wide">Discovery<span class="os-accent">OS</span>: One place to start every investigation.</h2><p class="body-text">Instead of asking PMs to choose where to look first, DiscoveryOS starts with their question.</p><p class="body-text">They can ask about a problem, trend, customer group, or product area. Bagel then uses the evidence it already has to surface areas worth looking into.</p><div class="img-frame" style="margin-top:48px"><img src="/images/bagelOS-05-discovery-start.png" style="border:2px solid black" alt="DiscoveryOS natural-language starting point"></div></section>
<section class="section"><span class="meta">06 · Product workflow</span><h2 class="cs-h2-wide">From a question to evidence</h2><div class="workflow-line">Ask → Surface → Explore → Validate</div><p class="body-text" style="margin-top:24px">The flow moves from an open question to the evidence behind a potential opportunity.</p><div class="walkthrough-grid"><article class="walkthrough-step"><span class="step-num">01 · Surface opportunities</span><h3 class="walkthrough-title">Turn an open question into a place to look.</h3><p class="body-text" style="margin-top:12px">Bagel uses the available customer evidence to surface themes and opportunities related to the PM's question.</p><div class="img-frame"><video src="/videos/bagelOS-06-surface-opportunities.mov" style="border:2px solid black" autoplay loop muted playsinline controls></video><div class="fig-cap">From an open question to a potential investigation.</div></div></article><article class="walkthrough-step"><span class="step-num">02 · Explore the insight</span><h3 class="walkthrough-title">See what's behind it.</h3><p class="body-text" style="margin-top:12px">PMs can open an opportunity, understand its impact, and inspect the evidence behind it.</p><div class="img-frame"><video src="/videos/bagelOS-07-explore-insight.mov" style="border:2px solid black" autoplay loop muted playsinline controls></video><div class="fig-cap">Opportunity, insight, and evidence in one flow.</div></div></article></div></section>
<section class="section-alt design-decisions"><span class="meta">07 · Design principles</span><h2 class="cs-h2-wide">Design decisions</h2><div class="feat-split design-principle principle-one" style="margin-top:48px"><div><span class="decision-mono">Principle 01</span><h3 class="walkthrough-title">Hierarchy over navigation</h3><p class="body-text" style="margin-top:16px">I structured the experience around:<br><br>Question → Opportunity → Insight → Evidence<br><br>Each step goes deeper into the same investigation instead of sending the PM to another part of the product.</p></div><div class="img-frame"><img src="/images/bagelOS-08-hierarchy-over-navigation.png" alt="Hierarchy from question to evidence"></div></div><div class="feat-split design-principle" style="margin-top:56px"><div class="img-frame"><img src="/images/bagelOS-09-act-on-insight.png" alt="Contextual actions available on an insight"></div><div><span class="decision-mono">Principle 02</span><h3 class="walkthrough-title">Act without leaving the investigation</h3><p class="body-text" style="margin-top:16px">When an insight is useful, PMs can create a new Idea or connect it to an existing one directly from the insight.</p></div></div><div class="feat-split design-principle" style="margin-top:56px"><div><span class="decision-mono">Principle 03</span><h3 class="walkthrough-title">Ask AI in context</h3><p class="body-text" style="margin-top:16px">Follow-up questions sit next to the evidence they relate to. For example, from a list of related product features, a PM can ask which ones are already in development.</p><p class="body-text">They don't have to open a separate chat and explain the context again.</p></div><div class="img-frame"><img src="/images/bagelOS-10-contextual-ai.png" alt="Contextual AI follow-up within an investigation"></div></div><div class="feat-split design-principle" style="margin-top:56px"><div class="img-frame"><img src="/images/bagelOS-11-living-artifact.png" alt="Widget library for a living insight artifact"></div><div><span class="decision-mono">Principle 04</span><h3 class="walkthrough-title">One source of truth</h3><p class="body-text" style="margin-top:16px">The insight stays up to date as new evidence comes in. PMs and stakeholders can rely on the same view when they share the investigation.</p><p class="body-text">It is built on the latest evidence, not a snapshot that goes stale.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><span class="meta">08 · Final product</span><h2 class="cs-h2-wide">One workflow from question to evidence.</h2><p class="body-text">DiscoveryOS brought the separate parts of Discovery into one place. PMs could start with a question, find something worth investigating, examine the evidence, and turn it into an Idea when it was ready.</p><div class="img-frame" style="margin-top:48px"><img src="/images/bagelOS-12-final-discoveryos.png" style="border:2px solid black" alt="Complete DiscoveryOS investigation experience"></div><div style="margin-top:56px"><span class="meta">09 · Outcomes</span><div class="outcomes-bold"><div class="outcome-item"><div class="outcome-stat">1 flow</div><div class="outcome-label">Four separate Discovery spaces brought into one experience</div></div><div class="outcome-item"><div class="outcome-stat">Validated</div><div class="outcome-label">The new workflow and product direction were validated with customers</div></div><div class="outcome-item"><div class="outcome-stat">5× growth</div><div class="outcome-label">Enterprise customer-base growth within three months*</div></div></div><p class="outcome-footnote">*Enterprise growth was shared by the founders following launch. Multiple factors contributed to this outcome.</p></div></section>
<section class="closing"><div class="closing-kicker">Final learning</div><p class="closing-quote">AI should support the decision, not make it.<br><em>Give people the context, evidence, and tools to reach their own conclusions.</em></p></section>
</body></html>
